LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Skimming"
English price skimming takes its metaphor from skimming cream off the top of milk: the seller takes the richest part of the market first and then works down. It has nothing to do with the other financial sense of skimming, which is the theft of small amounts from takings, and nothing to do with skimming a document. Arabic التسعير الكاشط keeps the idea of scraping the surface layer. French écrémage is the same dairy metaphor as the English, and écrémer is used in business speech exactly as the English verb is. The companion term is the clearer of the two in every language: penetration pricing means pushing into a market, and the image of entering rather than taking from the top is worth keeping in mind when deciding which strategy a question describes.
